# Project-internal working notes: remediation ledger, review correspondence,
# phase plans and verification records. Useful while the study was being built,
# not part of the released research artifact.
_internal/

# Secrets — never commit credentials
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Bulky regenerable artifacts: per-episode score dumps (npz). Everything the
# paper cites (tables, figures, results.json) IS committed; scores regenerate
# deterministically from the committed code + data.
results/scores/
results/*/scores/

# Scratch output of the behavioural tripwire (devtools/behavior_snapshot.py);
# the snapshot it compares against lives in tests/baseline/ and IS committed.
results/seed424242/

# Test / tooling caches
.pytest_cache/

# NOTE (baseline freeze 2026-07-16): trace datasets (traces/**) are now
# COMMITTED on purpose — they cost real API money to collect, are not
# regenerable deterministically, and the frozen baseline must pin
# "same dataset, same splits" for every future comparison.

# LaTeX build products (main.tex + references.bib + neurips.sty are the sources).
# The two manuscript PDFs are now build products too, not committed artifacts:
# they are regenerated from committed sources with latexmk and were only
# churning the history. paper/paper.tex is generated from paper/paper.md by
# devtools/md_to_latex.py and stays committed, so both PDFs rebuild from a
# clean checkout with no manual steps. See REPRODUCE.md for the commands.
paper/main.pdf
paper/paper.pdf
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.blg
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.synctex.gz

# Ephemeral disposable-seed study output (never published)
results/seed4242*/
results/seed9090*/
# Sensitivity-arm tree (AGENTWATCH_RESULTS_ROOT): runs the published seeds
# under non-published settings, deleted by its runner on success.
results/_sensitivity/

# LaTeX build artifacts
paper/main.fls
paper/main.fdb_latexmk
paper/paper.fls
paper/paper.fdb_latexmk
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.blg
paper/*.fdb_latexmk
paper/*.fls

# LaTeX build by-products from typesetting the manuscript.
*.log
*.aux
*.out
*.synctex.gz
!results/**/*.log

# Scratch images kept beside the repo (slide exports, generated previews).
# Published diagrams live in assets/ and ARE committed; mermaid diagrams stay
# inline in DESIGN.md, where they are diffable and cannot drift out of sync
# with the code the way an exported image can.
docs/

# Scratch output of `collect_traces --mock-llm`: scripted pipeline-test traces,
# deliberately kept out of the committed corpora they must never overwrite.
traces/_mock_dry_run/
traces/_smoke/

# Externally imported corpus (derail.experiments.import_aftraj): AFTraj-2K is
# another project's data under CC-BY-4.0. It is fetched on demand for the
# external-validation run and never redistributed from here.
traces/_aftraj/
traces/_atbench/

# Release payload for the Hugging Face dataset (devtools/hf_dataset.py). It is
# a derived copy of traces/ plus a generated card; committing it would store
# the corpus twice and let the copy drift from the record.
build/

# The NeurIPS workshop submission is under double-blind review. It is
# anonymised, and a public copy in a repository under the author's own name
# defeats that, so the source, the built PDF and the venue style file are kept
# out of the published tree until notification. They still build locally:
#   cd paper && latexmk -pdf workshop.tex
# NOTE: earlier commits still contain them; removing them from HEAD does not
# remove them from history.
paper/workshop.tex
paper/workshop.pdf
paper/neurips_2026.sty

# The TMLR submission, same reasoning. TMLR states that non-anonymous
# submissions are rejected without review, so the source and the built PDF stay
# out of the published tree until notification. It builds locally:
#   cd paper && latexmk -pdf tmlr.tex
# The style files below are the official TMLR package (Apache-2.0), vendored so
# the build works offline; they are not ours to redistribute here.
paper/tmlr.tex
paper/tmlr.pdf
paper/tmlr.sty
paper/tmlr.bst
paper/fancyhdr.sty
paper/math_commands.tex

# Deck build products: deck/build.py regenerates both from the template in
# seconds, and the inlined HTML is ~4 MB of base64 that churns on every edit.
deck/theory_2min.html
deck/theory_2min.pdf
